<VI _name="pa_insert_series_branch.vi" description="Kit helper (branch-safe variant of pa_insert_series2.xml\2C measured on an Actor Core 2026-10). Inserts a hook subVI IN SERIES on one or two panel wires of an override, in front of ONE named far terminal only, and keeps every other branch of that wire on the panel terminal. The kit helper reconnects only one far end after it deletes the wire; on an Actor Core whose class wire also feeds the helper loop, the stop frame and close, that drops three branches. Per block (A, then B if 'panel name B' is given): reads the wire leaving the panel terminal and all its terminals; the one named 'far name' whose owner's Class Name is 'far owner class' (default CallParentNode; a tunnel terminal carries its source's name, so the name alone is not enough) is the far end, all others (tunnels, other nodes) are kept; deletes the wire; wires panel -&gt; hook in, hook out -&gt; far end, and panel -&gt; each kept terminal again. Terminals matched by NAME. Then Save.Instrument of the VI (run pa_save_member afterwards for the class). Project OPEN and ACTIVE.">
